{{fbdoc item="title" value="NOINLINE"}}----
Disables procedure inlining in the C backends

{{fbdoc item="syntax"}}##
	[[KeyPgDeclare|Declare]] [[KeyPgFunction|Function]] //identifier// (//parameters//) [[KeyPgAs|As]] //return_type// **NoInline**
	[[KeyPgFunction|Function]] //identifier// (//parameters//) [[KeyPgAs|As]] //return_type// **NoInline**
	[[KeyPgDeclare|Declare]] [[KeyPgSub|Sub]] //identifier// (//parameters//) **NoInline**
	[[KeyPgSub|Sub]] //identifier// (//parameters//) **NoInline**
##

{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	##NoInline## follows the complete procedure signature, including a function's result type. It precedes ##[[KeyPgStatic|Static]]## and ##[[KeyPgExport|Export]]## on a definition. A declaration carrying the modifier passes it to the matching definition. A definition can also add the modifier to an earlier declaration.

	The ##-gen gcc## and ##-gen clang## backends emit the native ##noinline## function attribute. This can preserve a call boundary required by an imported C library's optimization policy. Native assembly backends already emit separate procedure bodies.

	The modifier applies to module procedures and member procedures. Calling conventions, parameter types and procedure-pointer compatibility retain their usual rules. ##NoInline## remains available as an identifier outside this position in a procedure header.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}%%(freebasic)
Declare Function adjust(ByVal value As Long) As Long NoInline

Function adjust(ByVal value As Long) As Long
    Return value + 3
End Function

Print adjust(4)
%%

{{fbdoc item="see"}}
	- [[KeyPgDeclare|Declare]]
	- [[KeyPgFunction|Function]], [[KeyPgSub|Sub]]
	- [[CompilerOptgen|Compiler option -gen]]

